{# ONE DAY OF ONE RANGER — the calendar tab's own cell, and the by-hand menu on it.

   THE CELL IS THE CALENDAR'S BAR. Owner, 21 sep: "it's even hard to look at
   it with all the colors and borders and everything on the shift pill", and
   "look at how clean the calendar is, as inspiration". So: a borderless
   tinted bar, a 5px dot, an 8px mono label — and nothing else.

   THE ONLY OUTLINED THING ON THE SHEET IS A GAP. An off day draws nothing at
   all, today is one tint down the column rather than an outline on each of
   thirty-four cells, and the alarm ink is spent on the one thing that needs
   a decision.

   A SHIFT'S COLOUR IS THE SHIFT'S. The cell reads the stored slot through
   `[data-cat]`, which the shell resolves — never a hue this module picked,
   and never a position in a list.

   THE MENU IS OPTION B, AND IT IS AN ACTION MENU. Owner: "the pop-up card
   for swaps could be designed better, otherwise it looks like a card with
   paragraphs, not actions." So it is the house dropdown's own panel with one
   verb per 30px row, a lucide mark, and no sentence anywhere: a fact about
   the day belongs on the cell, not in the menu. One line of facts on top and
   FIVE verbs under it — change the shift, move it, swap it, give the day off,
   clear the hand mark. There is no sixth: "mark the day unfilled" went with
   the cell kind it wrote, because a gap belongs to the station and not to a
   ranger.

   A VERB THAT TAKES A VALUE GROWS ITS CHOICE UNDER ITSELF. The area's shifts
   as chips, the station's rangers as a list — inline, in the same panel,
   because a second pop-up off a pop-up is two things to dismiss and nothing
   to read.

   THE MENU OPENS ON A DAY THERE IS SOMETHING TO DO WITH: a watch to move, or
   a mark to clear. An untouched off day has neither, and a menu of disabled
   items would be five ways of saying no. #}
{% set hasWatch = cell.dutyUuid is not null %}
{% set menu = mayPlan and (hasWatch or cell.editedByHand) %}
{#  THE CELL THAT OPENS A MENU IS A REAL BUTTON, and the event is named.
    Stimulus binds no default event to a `<span>`: the attribute renders,
    the controller connects, the cell is in its scope — and the click does
    nothing, which is exactly how this menu came to "open nothing" on a
    real click while every server-side test passed. A button also brings
    the keyboard with it, which a span never had. #}
{% set act = ' type="button" data-action="click->roster--day-menu#open"' %}
{% set dayRoute = path(constant('Uhifadhi\\Roster\\Controller\\RosterController::SHEET_DAY_ROUTE'), {uuid: area.uuid}) %}
{% set others = band.rows|filter(o => o.personUuid != row.personUuid) %}

{% if menu %}<span class="pmenuwrap">{% endif %}

{% if cell.kind.value == 'watch' %}
    <{{ menu ? 'button' : 'span' }} class="cl bar" data-cat="{{ cell.colour }}"{{ menu ? act|raw : '' }}><i class="dot"></i>{{ cell.shiftLabel|lower }}{% if cell.editedByHand %}<i class="hm" title="Edited by hand"></i>{% endif %}</{{ menu ? 'button' : 'span' }}>
{% else %}
    <{{ menu ? 'button' : 'span' }} class="cl off"{{ menu ? act|raw : '' }}>{% if cell.editedByHand %}<i class="hm" title="Given the day off by hand"></i>{% endif %}</{{ menu ? 'button' : 'span' }}>
{% endif %}

{% if menu %}
    <div class="pmenu dm" role="menu" aria-label="What to do with this day">
        {# THE CELL'S FACTS AS ONE LINE — who, which day, which shift, with
           the shift's own swatch. Not a heading over a card: the line the
           reader needs to be sure they opened the right cell. #}
        <span class="dmhd">
            <i class="sw" data-cat="{{ cell.colour }}"></i><b>{{ row.personName }}</b>
            &middot; {{ cell.day.format('D j')|lower }}
            {%- if cell.shiftLabel %} &middot; {{ cell.shiftLabel|lower }}{% endif %}
        </span>

        {% if hasWatch %}
            {# CHANGE THE SHIFT — the area's own shifts, as chips. #}
            <button type="button" class="dmr" role="menuitem" aria-expanded="false" data-action="roster--day-menu#step" data-roster--day-menu-step-param="shift">
                {{ ux_icon('roster:replace') }}<span class="l">Change the shift</span>
            </button>
            <form class="dmstep" method="post" action="{{ dayRoute }}" data-step="shift" hidden>
                <input type="hidden" name="_token" value="{{ csrfToken }}">
                <input type="hidden" name="op" value="shift">
                <input type="hidden" name="duty" value="{{ cell.dutyUuid }}">
                <input type="hidden" name="weeks" value="{{ window.weeks }}">
                <input type="hidden" name="from" value="{{ window.from.format('Y-m-d') }}">
                {% for shift in shifts %}
                    <button type="submit" name="shift" value="{{ shift.key }}" class="{{ shift.key == cell.shiftKey ? 'on' : '' }}"><i data-cat="{{ shift.colour }}"></i>{{ shift.label|lower }}</button>
                {% endfor %}
            </form>

            {# MOVE TO SOMEONE ELSE — stationed here, as a list. #}
            <button type="button" class="dmr" role="menuitem" aria-expanded="false" data-action="roster--day-menu#step" data-roster--day-menu-step-param="move">
                {{ ux_icon('roster:user-round-plus') }}<span class="l">Move to someone else</span>
            </button>
            <form class="dmstep who" method="post" action="{{ dayRoute }}" data-step="move" hidden>
                <input type="hidden" name="_token" value="{{ csrfToken }}">
                <input type="hidden" name="op" value="move">
                <input type="hidden" name="duty" value="{{ cell.dutyUuid }}">
                <input type="hidden" name="weeks" value="{{ window.weeks }}">
                <input type="hidden" name="from" value="{{ window.from.format('Y-m-d') }}">
                {% for other in others %}
                    <button type="submit" name="person" value="{{ other.personUuid }}">{{ other.personName }}</button>
                {% else %}
                    <span class="dmnone">nobody else is stationed here</span>
                {% endfor %}
            </form>

            {# SWAP WITH ANOTHER — offered, not applied: the other person
               accepts it on the handset, and the sheet shows both cells
               exchanged after that. #}
            <button type="button" class="dmr" role="menuitem" aria-expanded="false" data-action="roster--day-menu#step" data-roster--day-menu-step-param="swap">
                {{ ux_icon('roster:arrow-right-left') }}<span class="l">Swap with another</span>
            </button>
            <form class="dmstep who" method="post" action="{{ path(constant('Uhifadhi\\Roster\\Controller\\RosterController::OFFER_SWAP_ROUTE'), {uuid: area.uuid}) }}" data-step="swap" hidden>
                <input type="hidden" name="_token" value="{{ csrfToken }}">
                <input type="hidden" name="duty" value="{{ cell.dutyUuid }}">
                {% for other in others %}
                    <button type="submit" name="taking" value="{{ other.personUuid }}">{{ other.personName }}</button>
                {% else %}
                    <span class="dmnone">nobody else is stationed here</span>
                {% endfor %}
            </form>

            {# AND THE THREE THAT TAKE NO VALUE. #}
            <form method="post" action="{{ dayRoute }}" class="dmacts">
                <input type="hidden" name="_token" value="{{ csrfToken }}">
                <input type="hidden" name="duty" value="{{ cell.dutyUuid }}">
                <input type="hidden" name="weeks" value="{{ window.weeks }}">
                <input type="hidden" name="from" value="{{ window.from.format('Y-m-d') }}">

                <button type="submit" class="dmr" role="menuitem" name="op" value="off">
                    {{ ux_icon('roster:circle-slash') }}<span class="l">Give the day off</span>
                </button>
                {% if cell.editedByHand %}
                    <button type="submit" class="dmr" role="menuitem" name="op" value="clear">
                        {{ ux_icon('roster:eraser') }}<span class="l">Clear the hand mark</span>
                    </button>
                {% endif %}
            </form>
        {% elseif cell.editedByHand %}
            {# CLEARING THE MARK IS AN ACT OF ITS OWN, and the common case
               has no duty left to hang it on: the commonest edit is taking
               somebody OFF a watch, and the mark has to survive the thing
               it protects. So it posts the day itself. #}
            <form method="post" action="{{ path(constant('Uhifadhi\\Roster\\Controller\\RosterController::SHEET_CLEAR_MARK_ROUTE'), {uuid: area.uuid}) }}" class="dmacts">
                <input type="hidden" name="_token" value="{{ csrfToken }}">
                <input type="hidden" name="station" value="{{ band.stationUuid }}">
                <input type="hidden" name="person" value="{{ row.personUuid }}">
                <input type="hidden" name="day" value="{{ cell.day.format('Y-m-d') }}">
                <input type="hidden" name="weeks" value="{{ window.weeks }}">
                <input type="hidden" name="from" value="{{ window.from.format('Y-m-d') }}">
                <button type="submit" class="dmr" role="menuitem">
                    {{ ux_icon('roster:eraser') }}<span class="l">Clear the hand mark</span>
                </button>
            </form>
        {% endif %}
    </div>
{% endif %}

{% if menu %}</span>{% endif %}
